# Plan: Design Audit HUD Prototype

## Context

Building a premium interactive document audit system integrated into the NUDIMMUD HUD. The operator opens a Design Catalog, picks visual/interaction options, confirms the config, and is taken into a full Document Audit HUD that reflects those choices. The prototype also generates an exportable `NUDIMMUD_DESIGN_HANDOFF` JSON payload for downstream use (ChatGPT handoff, next design cycle).

**Why**: First test prototype for a larger "Design Architect" system. Must feel like a premium game customization screen, not a dashboard.

**Stack confirmed**: React 19 + Vite 5 + TypeScript, Framer Motion 12, Three.js (passive background). No Tailwind. CSS custom properties via ALBEDO DESIGN SYSTEM tokens in `index.css`. Module routing via `mountModule()` switch in `src/index.tsx`.

---

## Rendering Strategy

**App-integrated React component** — NOT standalone HTML.

The existing `mountModule()` switch in `src/index.tsx` accepts a string key and renders the matching React component into `#module-content`. Adding `case 'DESIGN_AUDIT'` slots in cleanly with zero plumbing changes. All design tokens, fonts, Framer Motion, and Three.js context are already live — no re-implementation needed.

